<mxfile host="65bd71144e">
    <diagram id="kaggleAdaptation01" name="Page-1">
        <mxGraphModel dx="1491" dy="755" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1460" pageHeight="1068" math="0" shadow="0">
            <root>
                <mxCell id="0"/>
                <mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>
                <mxCell id="k-title" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1;" value="Strong inference on a Kaggle competition: levers outside, puzzles inside" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="6" width="700" height="28" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-unchanged" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;fontSize=12;align=left;fontColor=#666666;fontStyle=2;" value="Unchanged from the base and not redrawn: the cycle's steps, the tree, the finding path, the branch gate. A rung's outcome follows the base's mapping onto 'What survives?'. See strong_inference_workflow.drawio." vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="1043" width="1300" height="22" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-k0" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;b&gt;K0. The competition fixes the objective&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Metric; target and its margin above the board; deadline; hard caps (GPU hours, money); submission form (a notebook, internet off, time limit); the board's band, inside which two public scores are the same result; final-selection rule written before the first submission: within the band of the best public score, the highest local. Never the public score alone." vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="50" width="245" height="192" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-k0n" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;fontSize=12;fontColor=#666666;fontSize=11;" value="Submissions per day and calendar time are watched, not sized against." vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="244" width="215" height="46" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-k1" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=13;dashed=1;" value="&lt;b&gt;K1. Frontier baseline (support work)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;A person builds a running baseline at or near the best public result that fits the caps. Not a hypothesis. Nothing below its rung is a question." vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="290" width="245" height="124" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-k2" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;b&gt;K2. Seed the ledger from public ablations&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Each public contribution enters as settled under other conditions: a candidate rung with a size, not knowledge. The reading asks per lever: has someone measured it, what size would it predict here, which levers are missing." vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="428" width="245" height="165" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-record" parent="1" style="shape=cylinder3;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;boundedLbl=1;backgroundOutline=1;size=18;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;b&gt;Loop record&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;The base's five rows (gain ratio, misses with cause, noise floor per family, rescues, cost ratio) plus two: pairs per regime, each with its deviation from the regime's offset; looks per adoption on the dev set. Offset and tolerance: the phase's record." vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="335" y="230" width="230" height="175" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-ledger" parent="1" style="shape=cylinder3;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;boundedLbl=1;backgroundOutline=1;size=18;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;b&gt;Lever ledger&lt;/b&gt; (a view of the tree: every lever is a question)&lt;br&gt;A lever is a named thing that can be changed and measured. Per lever: public size and source; local size; saturation (the gain of its last two runs against twice the family's floor); cost per point; status open, parked, saturated or blocked." vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="335" y="425" width="230" height="235" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-l1" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;b&gt;L1. Pick the next lever question&lt;/b&gt; (step 3, kind: lever)&lt;br&gt;Two open lever questions on different levers while the ledger holds two unsaturated levers; no branch over half of what remains; a plan whose worst case exceeds what remains of a hard cap is cut. Gain shown discounted by the loop record, cost corrected." vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="335" y="60" width="415" height="130" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-l2" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;b&gt;L2. One rung&lt;/b&gt;: one hypothesis, prediction with size and cost, the placeholder, no rival tree. Run it through base steps 5 to 9. The outcome table excludes only below the prediction minus the family's noise floor; between is undecided." vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="840" y="60" width="250" height="135" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-g1" parent="1" style="rhombus;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=13;" value="What survives? (this rung)" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="870" y="250" width="190" height="100" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-g2" parent="1" style="rhombus;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=13;" value="Second missed rung on the same lever?" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="630" y="240" width="210" height="120" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-l3" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;b&gt;L3.&lt;/b&gt; Base step 10 for a rung: store what holds, update the ledger with the measured gain" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="865" y="368" width="200" height="62" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-c1" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;b&gt;C1. Submit every clean rung&lt;/b&gt; once its first verdict is written, whatever it is; only the day's submissions and the hard caps limit it. Each yields a pair: local estimate before, public score after, tagged by family and regime. Writes the pairs row." vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="1160" y="60" width="280" height="118" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-gfirst" parent="1" style="rhombus;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=13;" value="First pair in this regime?" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="1210" y="193" width="180" height="100" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-c2" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;b&gt;C2.&lt;/b&gt; That pair is the regime's calibration: offset and tolerance (first guess 0.03) written to the protocol's record." vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="1160" y="315" width="240" height="85" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-gtol" parent="1" style="rhombus;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=13;" value="Inside tolerance?" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="1180" y="425" width="200" height="100" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-gtol-note" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;fontSize=12;fontSize=11;" value="Inside when the absolute deviation from the regime's offset is below the tolerance; on the edge counts as outside." vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="1290" y="530" width="150" height="84" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-frame" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=2;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#999999;dashed=1;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=8;fontStyle=2;fontColor=#666666;fontSize=13;" value="Inner loop: strong inference on a puzzle" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="630" y="610" width="510" height="230" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-trig" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;b&gt;Three triggers&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;A second missed rung on one lever; a pair outside tolerance; a plateau where the public work says there is room." vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="645" y="640" width="230" height="105" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-rivals" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;b&gt;Calibration puzzle's stock rivals&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Leakage through the split, drift in the training data, class-prior shift, regime inflation, public-set noise." vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="890" y="640" width="235" height="105" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-base" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=13;" value="The base cycle, steps 4 to 9, with branch budget and the gate 'Branch progressing?'. See strong_inference_workflow.drawio." vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="645" y="760" width="480" height="62" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-surv" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;b&gt;Survivor:&lt;/b&gt; goes on to the base's step 10, a measured use; what is measured there updates the ledger, then back to L1.&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:11px&quot;&gt;Cause is public-set noise: the lever is adopted at this exit. Any other cause: the rung is re-measured under the corrected protocol first.&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="632" y="848" width="240" height="116" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-parked" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;b&gt;Parked:&lt;/b&gt; back to L1 (base rule: Parked returns to step 3)&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:11px&quot;&gt;Adoption as for a survivor. A corroborated part may go to base step 10 (C3).&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="887" y="848" width="238" height="116" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-c3" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;b&gt;C3. Use of the cause (base step 10)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;A new phase; old exclusions keep their tag. A prediction about the first pair under it, with an outcome table; its failing row reopens the puzzle." vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="1180" y="898" width="260" height="130" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-plateau-lbl" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;fontSize=12;fontSize=11;fontColor=#b85450;" value="plateau where the public work says there is room" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="628" y="548" width="86" height="60" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-blk-lbl" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;fontSize=12;fontColor=#666666;fontSize=11;" value="the best estimate needs an asset that does not exist, or what a constraint forbids" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="335" y="661" width="235" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-blocked" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;b&gt;Blocked lever:&lt;/b&gt; still written, with the constraint or missing asset, expected gain and cost, and the proposal (for data: a cheap pilot, itself blocked under a constraint like D3)" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="335" y="702" width="235" height="125" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-person" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;b&gt;Person:&lt;/b&gt; lift a constraint, lower the target, or stop" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="335" y="855" width="235" height="60" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-obj" parent="1" style="rhombus;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=13;" value="Objective met, budget spent, or objective wrong?" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="622" width="240" height="125" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-stop" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=50;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;b&gt;Stop:&lt;/b&gt; final selection by the rule from K0. When the reason is 'objective wrong', the report lists blocked levers with constraint and gain." vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="25" y="775" width="230" height="115" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-obj-wrong" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;fontSize=12;fontColor=#9673a6;fontSize=11;" value="objective wrong" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="270" y="795" width="64" height="36" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-really" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=13;fontSize=12;" value="&lt;b&gt;Really trying:&lt;/b&gt; 'objective wrong' fires only when every lever is saturated, parked or blocked, the reading has been run at least twice for 'no path reaches' since the last lever was added and found nothing, and no open puzzle has budget left." vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="905" width="300" height="118" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-legend" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=3;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#999999;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=8;fontSize=12;" value="&lt;b&gt;Legend&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="1150" y="690" width="290" height="205" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-lg0" parent="1" style="fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;rounded=1;arcSize=8;html=1;" value="" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="1160" y="726" width="24" height="14" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
                <mxCell id="k-lgt0" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;fontSize=12;align=left;fontSize=11;" value="step" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="1188" y="718" width="108" height="30" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
